    "https://www.thiel.edu/offices/human-resources/adjunct-instructors-in-math": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructors in Math",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructors in Math - Thiel College Offices Apply Visit Deposit Aid & Tuition Give + This Section Menu About Degrees Admission Athletics Campus Life Alumni Apply Visit Give Aid & Tuition Directory Offices Calendar ABOUT ACADEMICS ADMISSION ATHLETICS CAMPUS LIFE ALUMNI OFFICES Academic Affairs Business Office College Advancement Communications & Marketing Events and Conferences Financial Aid Human Resources Employment Student Employment Staff Information Technology Facilities President's Office Student Accounts Student Life Human Resources Jennifer Clark Director of Human Resources jclark@thiel.edu 724-589-2858 Roth Memorial Hall Adjunct Instructors in Math Thiel College invites applications from qualified individuals to join our adjunct instructor pool in the Department of Math and Computer Science. We are actively building a roster of adjunct faculty available to teach on a course-by-course basis in the Spring 2027 semester and beyond. Two introductory quantitative reasoning courses are in need of coverage in spring 2027. Qualifications A master’s      degree in math, education, or a related field is required. A minimum      of two years of teaching experience is preferred. In-person      instruction at our Greenville, Pennsylvania campus is preferred; however,      remote options including synchronous online delivery are available for      qualified candidates. Why Thiel? Thiel College is an independent liberal arts college rooted in the Lutheran tradition. Thiel College empowers individuals to reach their full potential by creating a diverse and inclusive learning environment that ensures educational excellence, stimulates global awareness, and promotes ethical leadership. In doing so, Thiel prepares students for careers and lives of meaning and purpose. Thiel College welcomes applications from all qualified candidates. Please note, however, that we are unable to provide employment visa sponsorship (e.g., H-1B) for this position. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without current or future sponsorship. To apply, submit a letter of interest, CV, and contact information for three professional references as a single PDF document (titled with your last name) by clicking here . Applications are reviewed on a rolling basis. Visit www.thiel.edu to learn more about Thiel College. Thiel is committed to attracting a culturally and professionally diverse faculty and staff who engage students through rich curricular and cocurricular experiences. EOE Thiel College 75 College Ave Greenville, PA 16125 1-800-248-4435 Accessibility Public Safety Privacy Statement Fast Facts Student Consumer Information Disclosure Campus Directory Employment Title IX More Quick Links × Webmail Campus Offices Directory Schedule an Event Maintenance Issue Spectrum U IT Support Academic Catalog Academic Resources Accessibility Attend & Assist Boodlebox Buy Books Calendar Campus Map Handshake Course List Library The Learning Commons Moodle Newsroom Public Safety Self Service Solution Center Pay My Bill Thiel Gear Tomcats Care Wellness Center Close"
    },
    "https://www.thiel.edu/offices/human-resources/clinical-nursing-adjunct": {
      "title": "Clinical Adjunct Nursing Instructor",
      "description": "Clinical Adjunct Nursing Instructor - Thiel College Offices Apply Visit Deposit Aid & Tuition Give + This Section Menu About Degrees Admission Athletics Campus Life Alumni Apply Visit Give Aid & Tuition Directory Offices Calendar ABOUT ACADEMICS ADMISSION ATHLETICS CAMPUS LIFE ALUMNI OFFICES Academic Affairs Business Office College Advancement Communications & Marketing Events and Conferences Financial Aid Human Resources Employment Student Employment Staff Information Technology Facilities President's Office Student Accounts Student Life Human Resources Jennifer Clark Director of Human Resources jclark@thiel.edu 724-589-2858 Roth Memorial Hall Clinical Adjunct Nursing Instructor Thiel College seeks vibrant candidates to serve as adjunct faculty in our baccalaureate level Nursing program. Faculty collaborate with the Program Director to support the program’s mission and ensure compliance with CCNE accreditation standards.  A dedicated passion for helping students reach their full potential in a supportive and inclusive environment is essential to this position. Responsibilities primarily include teaching and student supervision. Qualifications: Teaching in a higher education setting is preferred but not required; effective communication and collaborative skills in a team-oriented environment and a history of successful time management Med/Surg nursing experience required Psych or pediatric nursing experience preferred, other specialty areas welcome A Master’s degree in Nursing from an accredited program is required; Ph.D or D.N.P preferred. Candidates who are near completion of their Master’s degree in Nursing will also be considered Must have current unencumbered RN license in Pennsylvania Knowledge of BSN-level assessment of clinical education preferred Essential Functions: Teach assigned courses within our Nursing Program to meet lab and clinical needs Contribute to curriculum development to ensure student learning objectives are met Monitor student progress and contribute to remediation when necessary Assist with CCNE accreditation activities Maintain licensure and/or certification To Apply: Thiel College welcomes applications from all qualified candidates. Please note, however, that we are unable to provide employment visa sponsorship (e.g., H-1B) for this position.  Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without current or future sponsorship. Qualified applicants should please submit a cover letter, resume, and the contact information for three professional references by clicking here . All application materials should be attached in a single PDF document using candidate’s name (Lname, Fname) as the document title.  For additional information, please contact Dr. Debra Wallace dwallace@thiel.edu . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until positions are filled. Thiel College is committed to attracting a culturally and professionally diverse faculty and staff who engage our students by providing a rich and fulfilling curricular and co-curricular experience. Thiel College 75 College Ave Greenville, PA 16125 1-800-248-4435 Accessibility Public Safety Privacy Statement Fast Facts Student Consumer Information Disclosure Campus Directory Employment Title IX More Quick Links × Webmail Campus Offices Directory Schedule an Event Maintenance Issue Spectrum U IT Support Academic Catalog Academic Resources Accessibility Attend & Assist Boodlebox Buy Books Calendar Campus Map Handshake Course List Library The Learning Commons Moodle Newsroom Public Safety Self Service Solution Center Pay My Bill Thiel Gear Tomcats Care Wellness Center Close"
    },
    "https://www.thiel.edu/offices/human-resources/adjunct-professor-of-history": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor of History",
      "description": "Adjunct Professor of History - Thiel College Offices Apply Visit Deposit Aid & Tuition Give + This Section Menu About Degrees Admission Athletics Campus Life Alumni Apply Visit Give Aid & Tuition Directory Offices Calendar ABOUT ACADEMICS ADMISSION ATHLETICS CAMPUS LIFE ALUMNI OFFICES Academic Affairs Business Office College Advancement Communications & Marketing Events and Conferences Financial Aid Human Resources Employment Student Employment Staff Information Technology Facilities President's Office Student Accounts Student Life Human Resources Jennifer Clark Director of Human Resources jclark@thiel.edu 724-589-2858 Roth Memorial Hall Adjunct Professor of History Thiel College invites applications from qualified individuals to serve as Adjunct Professor of History in the Spring 2027 semester, teaching the US History survey and a 200-level US history course, with topic flexible. Candidates are welcome to propose a course in their area of expertise in consultation with the department. Qualifications A      master's degree in history or a related field is required. A      minimum of two years of teaching experience is preferred. Candidates      with a strong background in U.S. history, and the ability to design an      upper-level topics course in their area of specialization, are preferred. In-person      instruction at our Greenville, Pennsylvania campus is required. Why Thiel? Thiel College is an independent liberal arts college rooted in the Lutheran tradition. Thiel College empowers individuals to reach their full potential by creating a diverse and inclusive learning environment that ensures educational excellence, stimulates global awareness, and promotes ethical leadership. In doing so, Thiel prepares students for careers and lives of meaning and purpose. Thiel College welcomes applications from all qualified candidates. Please note, however, that we are unable to provide employment visa sponsorship (e.g., H-1B) for this position. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without current or future sponsorship. To apply, submit a letter of interest, CV, and contact information for three professional references as a single PDF document (titled with your last name) by clicking here . Applications are reviewed on a rolling basis. Visit www.thiel.edu to learn more about Thiel College. Thiel is committed to attracting a culturally and professionally diverse faculty and staff who engage students through rich curricular and cocurricular experiences. EOE Thiel College 75 College Ave Greenville, PA 16125 1-800-248-4435 Accessibility Public Safety Privacy Statement Fast Facts Student Consumer Information Disclosure Campus Directory Employment Title IX More Quick Links × Webmail Campus Offices Directory Schedule an Event Maintenance Issue Spectrum U IT Support Academic Catalog Academic Resources Accessibility Attend & Assist Boodlebox Buy Books Calendar Campus Map Handshake Course List Library The Learning Commons Moodle Newsroom Public Safety Self Service Solution Center Pay My Bill Thiel Gear Tomcats Care Wellness Center Close"
